WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.840
- Hey guys, welcome to another installment

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.950
of Ask Doctor Mike.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.670
This time, all of the
questions are coming from you.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.890
So I'm really excited to
answer all of your questions.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:10.757
Let's get to it.

00:00:10.757 --> 00:00:14.940
- Gotta question, I just
recently got my wisdom teeth

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.940
taken out, and I have four
huge holes in my mouth.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.880
How can I get them to
close as quick as possible?

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.570
- Getting your wisdom teeth taken out

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.360
is definitely a painful experience.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.100
I had all four of mine taken out,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.560
and they were all impacted.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.230
It really did hurt, so I feel you.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.880
There is no secret way to
speed up the healing process.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.880
The best thing that you
can do is prevent infection

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.310
by keeping the area clean.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.550
Really what's the number one thing

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.390
that you shouldn't do is smoke.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.780
Smoking does prolong healing time,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.930
and that's the number one thing

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.170
that we talk to our
patients during surgeries

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.800
is that they should stop
smoking as soon as possible.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.850
- So I just found out that
I'm gluten intolerant.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.330
Can you explain what
is gluten intolerance,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.570
why it can happen, and what is the effect

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.960
to my body if I still consume gluten?

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.940
Can I eat like one, two, three, four

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.300
or five small bites
for a treat for myself?

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.620
Is it dangerous?

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:07.720
Thanks Doctor Mike.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.280
- Bella, gluten intolerance
is a very popular subject

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.290
right now, but the way that
I like to break it down

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.820
to my patients is that there's
two types of gluten issues.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.010
One is celiac disease, you've
heard about it in the news.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.840
And celiac disease is actual damage,

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.220
in your intestines, from eating gluten,

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.600
which is a protein byproduct of wheat.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.910
In celiac disease, when you consume wheat

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.790
your body has an auto-immune response.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.840
Which means that your own
body attacks its own cells

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.620
because of an over-reaction
to the wheat product,

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.020
and you get physical
damage in your intestines.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.110
Now, the second part of this is something

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.830
called non-celiac wheat sensitivity.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.840
There's people that
are sensitive to wheat,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.110
but not necessarily to
the gluten component.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.190
In non-celiac wheat sensitivity

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.030
we don't have the research to back up

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.440
what happens if you continue eating wheat.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.550
However, my opinion, you
should not eat wheat,

00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.870
because it's gonna make you feel better,

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.120
and you'll be in less of a fog.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.500
You'll have less diarrhea, less bloating.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.360
So if you do have symptoms
from eating wheat,

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.690
just don't eat it.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.770
Okay, that's a great question Faez,

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.630
and it really does give
strength to the statement

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.000
that you can die of too much of anything.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.480
So yes, you can die of
taking too much water

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.566
because you limit your body's ability

00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:22.180
to properly manage the
electrolytes within your system.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.390
Electrolytes are crucial for managing

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:27.080
everyday life functions,
like making your brain work,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.970
your heart work, or even your kidneys.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.760
- What do you recommend
for people with IBS,

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.280
'cause we both worry about our
intestines on a daily basis.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.400
Thanks Doctor Mike.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.000
- Hey girls, if you do
have IBS and it's true,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.760
treatment depends on which
type of IBS you have.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.750
There's IBS that's mostly
diarrhea-predominant.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.390
There's IBS constipation-predominant.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.230
And there's also a mixed version as well.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.420
For mild disease or symptoms you can do

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.400
some dietary modifications.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.670
There's a specific diet
that we put patients on

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:58.460
who suffer from IBS, called a FODMAP diet.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.010
What that diet does is
it excludes certain foods

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.090
that your body's unable to digest,

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.140
and the bacteria in your
stomach are able to digest.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.520
So it causes that uncomfortable
bloating feeling, pain,

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.520
and it really does mess
with your bowel movements.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.860
If you're able to eliminate
those types of foods,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.100
people do see an improvement
in their symptoms.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.270
If you do have a moderate or severe form

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.843
of the illness, there are medications

00:03:19.843 --> 00:03:21.850
that you can use to treat your illness.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.960
However, in order to
get those medications,

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.540
and to find out what medications

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.500
are suited best for your symptoms,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.410
it's important to go see your doctor.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.140
- Hi Doctor Mike, my question for you is

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.620
how can I improve my eczema,
because none of the products

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.640
that my dermatologists have
recommended towards me,

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.440
or pretty much anything that
I've been attempting to doing

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.670
hasn't really worked that well.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.830
What can I do myself,
like involving nutrition,

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.380
or stuff that I can kinda control

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.730
that's not super financially expensive.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.510
- Eczema's a very tricky illness,

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.270
and I understand your frustration.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:59.150
If you've already seen a
dermatologist they've probably

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.470
discussed some of the
treatment options with you.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.040
Talking about UV light
therapy, steroid creams,

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.650
maybe even medications that
affect your immune system.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.280
But like you said, those
are expensive modifications,

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.630
expensive treatments,

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.360
some of them do come with side-effects.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.970
Links between eczema flares and diet

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.930
has been a popular subject
that's been up for debate.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.760
It's not clear what the link is,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.210
but we certainly know
that a link does exist.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.180
I don't like recommending to my patients

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.580
eliminating certain
foods from their diets,

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.290
but this is a great time
to have a conversation

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.180
with your dermatologist or
your primary care doctor

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.470
to get tested for food allergies.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.500
Because there is a relationship

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.130
in those who have food allergies

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.660
to those who have worsening eczema.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.450
If you're able to find out early on

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.660
that you have a food
allergy, and you're able

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.680
to eliminate that specific
food from your diet,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.670
it's possible that your
eczema flares will decrease,

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.645
or at least that when they do
happen they won't be as bad.

00:04:53.645 --> 00:04:55.950
- Hey Doctor Mike, my question for you is

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.390
how and when did you know which area

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.010
of medicine you wanted to specialize in?

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.950
- I chose family medicine specifically,

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.370
because I love continuity of care.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.790
I love being able to communicate

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.570
with my patients every single day,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.880
and also I love not limiting myself

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.680
to focusing on one specific
body part or organ.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.160
I think the beauty of family medicine

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.340
lies in that I'm able to see the effect

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.090
my treatment has on my patient.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.100
I'm able to see how it
improves their lives,

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.950
and that's incredibly rewarding.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.220
- Hi Doctor Mike, I'm involved in a lot

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.490
of sporting activities, and I tend

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.200
to sprain my ankles when I play sports.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.530
I was wondering if there
is anything that I can do

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.810
to help strengthen my
ankles, like an exercise.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.110
That way I won't hurt
them as much as I do.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.520
- Hey Anna, the way that
you prevent ankle injuries

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.630
is through improving your proprioception,

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.930
which is your body's ability
to know where your limbs

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.170
are at all times, even
without seeing them.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.220
The best way to strengthen
your ankle and prevent injuries

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.540
is to do proprioception exercises.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.220
The first one that I want
all my patients to try

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.250
is to stand on one foot, of
course without a sneaker,

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.200
with their hands to
their sides, eyes open,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.590
and see how long they
could hold that position.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.790
Then to make the exercise a little harder,

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.860
you can take your arms and
put them at your sides,

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.500
which will make it, the balancing
a little more difficult.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.770
And then the next part, very challenging,

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.410
is to do the same thing with your arms

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.660
at your sides, but close your eyes

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.780
and see how long you
can hold that position.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.760
The longer you can hold that position

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.940
the less likely you are
to have an ankle injury.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.100
You can certainly see
your physical therapist

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.540
who will teach you more advanced exercises

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:27.190
and work with you directly
to prevent future injuries.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.380
I see, over and over
again, people claiming

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.000
that vitamin D's the
cure-all for all illnesses.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.710
And clearly it's not the case.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.380
There's been a huge uproar,
and uptick in studies,

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.950
and articles coming out recently

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.420
saying that Americans are
taking too much vitamin D now.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.130
I've said this maybe two months ago

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.950
in a YouTube video called
Are Vitamins Fake News?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.310
Check out that video and see
the real deal on vitamin D.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:52.740
- I would like it if you
could explain to people

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.260
why asthma has many different levels.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.940
Why some people find
one puff with an inhaler

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:00.300
will help them, and other
people with severe asthma

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.160
like myself need nebulizers
and oxygen therapy,

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:05.580
because I feel like
people still take asthma

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.400
as a bit of a joke, and they seem to think

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.340
that people with asthma are
hypochondriacs and things.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:15.260
I've spent many times in ICU,
I've been critically ill.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.550
I've had pleurisy, I've had many things

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.087
and I've been told by friends,

00:07:19.087 --> 00:07:20.967
"You know, if you're
gonna be making that noise

00:07:20.967 --> 00:07:22.700
"can you go home, 'cause
you're annoying me."

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.460
I've been asked if I could be quiet.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.740
And so, if you could maybe feature this

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.730
and answer the question,
that would be amazing.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.386
And I would really appreciate it because

00:07:31.386 --> 00:07:33.940
I feel like (laughs) I'm
talking to a brick wall

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.470
when I try to explain to people.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.210
Coming from a doctor it might be better.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.043
Thanks Mike.

00:07:38.043 --> 00:07:40.027
- First of all, to all those who said,

00:07:40.027 --> 00:07:42.730
"Asthma's a joke," they
are completely wrong,

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:43.940
they don't know what
they're talking about,

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.940
and I'm so sorry you
had to go through that.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.540
Asthma's a very serious illness

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.600
and I've had to intubate otherwise healthy

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.170
16-year-olds with the illness.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.510
There are levels to asthma,
you have mild asthma

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:55.540
moderate asthma and severe asthma.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:56.950
There's further classifications,

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.600
but that's for your doctor to worry about.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.377
And the difference between
the levels of asthma

00:08:00.377 --> 00:08:02.990
is the difference between
the types of medications

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.220
you need to take.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.200
So for the more severe
asthma, you're gonna need

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.040
to take controller medications,

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.770
ones to prevent asthma attacks

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.510
from happening in the first place.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.650
Versus for mild, intermittent asthma

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:16.990
you can just have a rescue
inhaler and use it as needed.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.370
You clearly have a more
advanced case of asthma,

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:21.840
so you do need to be on
a controller medication,

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.640
and I'm so sorry you had to go through

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.550
all of this ridicule from your friends,

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.400
because they don't know
what they're talking about.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.220
Alright guys it's time
for the lightening round.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.060
What is the healthiest way to burn fat?

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.150
HIIT, high intensity interval training.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:37.680
It's where you build muscle
and burn fat at the same time.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.840
How can I get fatter?

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:39.673
Really though?

00:08:39.673 --> 00:08:41.570
Well, you could sleep
less than six hours a day,

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.110
eat a ton of carbs and
be a huge couch potato.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.080
How to deal with insomnia.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.470
Insomnia's tricky because you need

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:50.140
to get a full history,
and a full physical exam,

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.180
and sometimes get some lab work done.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.250
Not an easy question to
answer, go see your doctor.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.150
If you weren't a doctor, what other career

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:57.170
would you have pursued?

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.210
Detective, I love investigating,

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.430
and that's frankly what I
do every day as a doctor.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:02.890
How do you remove eye bags?

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.410
Eye bags make me not confident, thanks.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.710
Eye bags can be removed with a cold spoon,

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.740
or fillers, I've seen some great results.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.520
What type of doctor are you?

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.497
Family medicine, the
best specialty out there.

00:09:13.497 --> 00:09:14.330
(bell pings)

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:17.030
What's the most challenging
part of being a doctor?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.220
Constantly refreshing your knowledge.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.760
Things change every single day,

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.390
and it's important that
you stay up-to-date.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.700
I really enjoyed answering
all of your questions today.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.520
I wasn't able to get to
all of the questions,

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.560
and if you still have something

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.260
that you're itching to learn about,

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:31.600
leave a comment down below,
I'll make sure to get to it.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.920
And I hope you're excited for the

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.717
next installment of Ask Doctor Mike.

